    "faq": {
      "type": "custom-accordion",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_firmness": {
          "type": "panel",
          "settings": {
            "summary": "How firm is the 4000 Ortho Elite?",
            "callout": "",
            "content": "<p>Firm orthopaedic tension, 9/10 — one of the firmest mattresses in the range. 4000 dual-layer pocket springs and stability-focused memory foam give a solid, supportive feel with minimal sink, rated for sleepers up to 20 stone.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_backpain": {
          "type": "panel",
          "settings": {
            "summary": "Is an orthopaedic mattress good for back pain?",
            "callout": "",
            "content": "<p>For many people, yes. It is designed to keep the spine aligned and stop hips and shoulders sinking out of position, a common cause of morning back pain. In our own customer data, 84.5% of firm-mattress shoppers came to us with back pain as their main concern. As non-medical professionals we make no guarantees — for personalised advice, speak to a GP or physiotherapist.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_vs_hybrid": {
          "type": "panel",
          "settings": {
            "summary": "What's the difference between this and a standard hybrid?",
            "callout": "",
            "content": "<p>Most hybrids use a single layer of pocket springs. This uses a dual-layer system that doubles the spring count for firmer, more stable support, with stability-focused memory foam on top to minimise sink. The result is a firmer, corrective feel rather than the medium feel of a standard hybrid.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_vs_5000": {
          "type": "panel",
          "settings": {
            "summary": "Should I choose the 4000 Ortho Elite or the 5000 Lux Elite?",
            "callout": "",
            "content": "<p>Choose the 4000 Ortho Elite for the firmest, orthopaedic-level support. If you want excellent support with a little more cushioning and pressure relief, the 5000 Lux Elite is medium-firm and the better fit. Side sleepers who need more give at the hips and shoulders may prefer the 3000 Supreme.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_trial": {
          "type": "panel",
          "settings": {
            "summary": "What happens if I try it and don't get on with it?",
            "callout": "",
            "content": "<p>It comes with a 100-night sleep trial — 200 nights with a protector — and a 15-year guarantee. If you return it during the trial, email us and we'll arrange free collection. Through our partnership with the British Heart Foundation, your returned mattress is sold through their stores with 100% of the proceeds supporting their work.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_springs": {
          "type": "panel",
          "settings": {
            "summary": "Why are REM-Fit springs different?",
            "callout": "",
            "content": "<p>We use tall pocket springs made from triple-tempered steel, each in its own fabric pocket so the springs never rub against each other. Tall springs give better support and isolate partner movement more effectively than mini springs alone, and sit deep enough beneath the comfort layers that you never feel them.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_base": {
          "type": "panel",
          "settings": {
            "summary": "What base can it go on?",
            "callout": "",
            "content": "<p>Any base, including adjustable, thanks to the high-density foam base layer. Slatted bases need slats no more than 10cm apart.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "faq_delivery": {
          "type": "panel",
          "settings": {
            "summary": "How long does delivery take?",
            "callout": "",
            "content": "<p>Free 2–5 day delivery to UK addresses by a two-person team, to your room of choice, delivered rolled and bagged. Old mattress recycling is available at checkout for a small fee.</p>",
            "open": false
          }
        }
      },
